  "disclosures": [
    {
      "id": "A6 wording superseded",
      "text": "The committed audit asked that shuffling the oracle make C \"collapse to B's coverage\". B's coverage is 98\u2013100 %, so no shuffle can produce that value: the direction is impossible. A6 is implemented as shuffled precision in B's measured band, shuffled coverage under A1's own 0.50 gate, and the shuffled transfer score not matching C's. The thresholds are the protocol's own; none was relaxed."
    },
    {
      "id": "three limbs, not four",
      "text": "\u00a73.4 says four scored windows; \u00a74.4 lists revision 200\u2013249 and a held-out 250\u2013299; the pinned runner scores three limbs. Three is what \u00a77's Bonferroni-over-three assumes. This harness scores retention 110\u2013149, transfer 150\u2013199 and revision 250\u2013299, and treats 200\u2013249 as the learning window it is."
    },
    {
      "id": "T1's regime switch",
      "text": "The T1 generator defaults to a law change at cycle 150, which would put the change inside the transfer window \u00a74.4 says is under the old law. The harness generates T1 with a switch at 200 and verifies the recorded regime at the boundary. The module default and \u00a74.4 disagree."
    },
    {
      "id": "A6 on T1 is not a control",
      "text": "T1's support covers 12 of 16 targets per source, so a size-matched wrong filter necessarily retains permitted pairs (the retained share is printed). A6 is therefore gated on the primary task T2 and reported as not applicable on T1. A control that cannot discriminate is not a passed control."
    },
    {
      "id": "bar selection",
      "text": "The comparators' configurations are frozen from the calibration artifact; only WHICH comparator is the bar per limb is chosen, on seed 20261099. Three comparators are fitted (replay, bigram, cell counter) rather than the protocol's two, which can only raise the bar."
    },
    {
      "id": "A2's scope",
      "text": "A2 is the committed audit on the arm's own stream: admitted = count-threshold-eligible pairs intersected with the support. A stronger C-versus-B comparison was implemented first and failed; it is reported as D1, not folded into A2. The strict comparison is kept because it measures whether the arms are independent, and it is not used to pass or fail the protocol."
    },
    {
      "id": "A3's band is T2's",
      "text": "The 0.3443 precision ceiling was measured on the compositional world. A3 applies it on T2 and reports T1's precision without gating, because T1 has no committed band. Applying a T2 constant to T1 would measure the wrong population."
    },
    {
      "id": "orientation of the decision difference",
      "text": "\u00a77 writes d = score(arm) \u2212 score(baseline) and calls a positive lower bound a win. With log-loss, lower is better, so the orientation that makes the rule coherent is d = baseline log-loss \u2212 arm log-loss. That is the quantity bootstrapped, and it is named in every artifact."
    }
  ],
